e head and body, only Mizutani was left as a suspect. Upon closer inspection, Mizutani also made some mistakes in some details. [4007] \"However, due to the strong impression caused by the Ito-Uma murder case, we overestimated the killer and thought that the killer would not easily leave clues. This was my mistake. [4008] \"But, Mizutani didn't take anything with her hands at that time, did she?\" [4009] I remember that Mounta had testified to this. [4010] \"She put them in her skirt. She wrapped them in a bag before putting them in. It is said that there were many such pickpocket gangs in America around ten years ago. They even stole medium-sized televisions, but the principle is the same. To an outsider, it looks like they didn't take anything.\" [4011] \"Akiba used this trick out of caution, which brought her good luck. As a result, her cautious adventure made her even further away from the circle of suspects. [4012] \"There is nothing remarkable afterwards. The initial murder took a lot of effort, no, the secret room was also purely accidental, and she chose a safe method afterwards. She was afraid that too much refinement would put her in danger. [4013] \"When killing Jouma, she held up the head of Tamekichi in the corridor. She wore a larger size of clothes and placed Tamekichi's head on her own head. There is a similar scene in the recently discovered tragedy of Aeschylus. I don't know if Akiba referred to it. Then, she made Yuzu see this scene, thus luring me to open Tamekichi's coffin. [4014] \"Wakaba and Kanae, as well as Jouma's murder, were almost untouched except for decapitation. [4015] \"In addition, discovering Hikari was a stroke of luck for Akiba. Otherwise, it would have been a great loss for her face.\" [4016] \"But there's Yuzuha too, right?\" [4017] \"No,\" Wakisugi denied, \"Yuzuha was part of Fujiko's murder plan from the beginning. However, Yuzuha was also lucky. Because just in the nick of time, Tomioka's relative, McArthur, appeared. [4018