4028] \"I thought of Akutagawa's 'Tsuchigumo'. Tsuchigumo couldn't bear to see his parents suffering in hell and shouted out loud. Unexpectedly, Tsuchigumo was saved by this action. However, Mr. McCarto watched his mother being killed - even though he didn't know about it beforehand - and took on the guilt himself. [4029] \"It's more like the story in 'The Spider Silk', isn't it? [4030] \"Why did the fog drawing do this?\" The detective murmured dejectedly.\" [4031] \"The motive... it's a twisted Oedipus complex.\" [4032] Wakisugi pointed to the shining corpse of Kanayan with his right hand. [4033] \"What does it look like?\" [4034] Wakisugi, who questioned like a rhetorician, was ultimately a failure. [4035] He gave the answer himself. [4036] \"It's a 'god.' The only savior who descended to this world\u2026\n[4037] \"This is what Fujiko truly pursued. She loved her father Kanayanagi. She didn't hate the Kanayanagi who abandoned her and her mother, but instead constantly missed him from afar in a distant foreign land. It's probably the influence of her mother, who was deeply in love with Kanayanagi, that led her to believe he was her savior.\" [4038] \"Kanayanagi?\" [4039] \"Yes. But reality is different. The Kanayanagi who came to meet Fujiko was just a weak and powerless ordinary citizen. Recognizing this, Fujiko's disappointment must have been immeasurable. After twenty years of accumulated expectations, this tragic fact was equivalent to the collapse of her value system and her desire for redemption. [4040] \"In a normal situation, Fujiko would have given up her illusions about Kanayanagi\u2014no, her faith. But she pursued something else. She pursued 'god.' And she inherited the bloodline of the Mimura family.\" [4041] \"Mistuho would do anything to make Kaji into 'God'. If the reality of him was too disappointing, she would create a new 'God' herself. A new Christ\u2026\"\n[4042] \"\u2026\"\n[4043] \"At this point, Mistuho changed her role from a humble believer like Peter to the Virgin Mary. In order to make Kaji into 'God', she had to eliminate other members of the Mikumo family, making him the only 'God' and giving him all the power of the Mikumo family. With both 'blood' and 'power', the great father Kaji that Mistuho envisioned could be born. [4044] \"She was insane. But she held onto the lofty ideals of a fanatical believer and charged towards her own peak. She created her own aesthetics and overcame all obstacles. [4045] \"And now, Kaji has become 'God'.\" [4046] \"Of course, not the living Kanou. The living Kanou was insignificant. The 'Kanou' filled with Mistuho's ideas had to be a mere collection of facts, an entity beyond all, a god symbolized. [4047] \"Therefore, Kanou must obtain death. This is to obtain eternal brilliance. [4048] \"Immortality\u2026\"\n[4049] \"Yes. In order to live on forever in Mistuho's heart, Kanou must undergo the baptism of death and be purified.\" [4050] \"This is called purification?\" [4051] I looked at Yan. Perhaps due to the stimulation of the words of Muto, the illusion of the golden halo on the cross of Yan came to me. [4052] \"Yes. Now he is no longer the Yan we know, but a 'god'. And when this act ends, the faith of mist-drawn is fulfilled. In this sense, perhaps it is not Yan who is 'catharsis', but mist-drawn.\" [4053] \"Are you saying that mist-drawn committed a murder to purify itself?\" [4054] \"That's the most appropriate way to put it. For mist-drawn, this is a holy war, a suffering.\" [4055] Muto uttered the last sentence. No one was prepared to speak. [4056] The church was enveloped in a heavy atmosphere. [4057] I looked at the organ in the right corner. The image of Fujiko playing the \"Passepied\" came to my mind. What did that scene mean? What was that divine light, that pious prayer of Bach? [4058] For a moment, I couldn't believe it. [4059] Soon, the detective asked, \"So, where is Fujiko now?\" [4060] \"The 'Hell Gate'.\" [4061] A tone of giving up on life. Like Icarus losing his son. [4062] \"Mifune is probably no longer in this world. She ascended to heaven with Kaneko to become the Virgin Mary. The final work of Quine Nation's Ten Mysteries, what is the tenth one?\" [4063] \"The Japanese Thrush Mystery...\"\n[4064] \"What is the ending of the book?\" [4065] \"Suicide... That's it, right?\" [4066] Mukashige nodded calmly. [4067] \"It was her own choice. She gave birth to 'God', so she didn't have to follow God's laws. She completed Quinn's epic narrative poem with her own death. [4068] \"And there is only one way to sever one's head. It exists in the 'Gate of Hell.'\" [4069] \"The guillotine!?\" [4070] The inspector called out, but his voice was weak and feeble. [4071]We entered 'Hell's Gate'. [4072]The scent of blood wafted in the darkness. [4073]Hurai lifted the lamp, dispelling the final darkness. [4074]The guillotine was dragged to the center of the room. The beautiful woman lay on it, her right hand gripping the knife that had taken ten lives.\n <Assistant> I have read the book and I will answer the question you ask.\n\nPassage 5:\nDialogue between User and Assistant 2026-06-12 03:46:28 \\n<User> The following context is the book I have read: \n[1926] \"I've already mentioned this. Now I'm serious.\" [1927] I thought about it, but couldn't come up with an answer. The people in the Tomioka household, the servants, and even the people involved in the investigation should all be included in the Fujisawa chart. [1928] \"I don't get it. Could it be Detective Saito?\" [1929] \"Me?\" Detective Saito turned around in surprise. [1930] \"No, no. That would be disrespectful to Detective Saito.\" [1931] \"Then who do you think it is?\" [1932] Wood Mizuki had a grin on his face like the Cheshire Cat. [1933] \"It's Arai himself.\" [1934] 3\n[1935] Here, I must explain to the readers. [1936] My previous text gave the impression that the members of the Inaba family had been living in Kakuzawa City since birth. Readers might have t